# Whether a callee is copied goes by the place of the call in the body that is built, and by the callee. Which functions lead back to the caller is a word on the rest of the program: with it a function would be compiled otherwise in a test than in the program that ships.
# `weigh`, nine operations of which one calls `log`, so that it is no leaf, is larger than its call. `visit` may be entered again from below itself, `once` may not: both call it. In the loop of `each` it is copied
